WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:54.340
<b>Stowaway</b>

3
00:01:52.580 --> 00:01:54.820
[HINA]
Yes, we sank one ship.

4
00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:57.560
Just one, belonging
to some Bon Clay,

5
00:01:57.590 --> 00:01:59.160
a Baroque Works agent.

6
00:01:59.190 --> 00:02:02.730
The other ship
was able to get away

7
00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:05.260
[SMOKER]
So you let them escape.

8
00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:08.540
[HINA]
To think that I fell
for such a cheap trick.

9
00:02:08.540 --> 00:02:10.900
[SMOKER]
Running away
is what they do best.

10
00:02:10.940 --> 00:02:12.110
[SUBORDINATE A grunts]
[MARINE GUARD grunts]

11
00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:15.670
Miss Hina, watch out!

12
00:02:15.670 --> 00:02:18.740
[HINA]
But it's so infuriating.
Hina's angry.

13
00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:20.250
[SMOKER]
Anger at your own incompetence?

14
00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:21.830
[SUBORDINATE A yells]

15
00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:25.520
[HINA]
No, that's not it.

16
00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:28.220
[SUBORDINATE A grunts]

17
00:02:28.240 --> 00:02:30.510
Whoa! Outstanding!

18
00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:32.230
Cage-Cage Fruit is intense!

19
00:02:32.260 --> 00:02:34.530
She has the power to
bind any part of the body

20
00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:35.570
she touches!

21
00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:36.360
There's a skill!

22
00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:37.630
C'mon, say it!

23
00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:39.170
Say the killer line just one time!

24
00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:42.370
[SUBORDINATE A groans]

25
00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:45.140
What the hell did you do to me?

26
00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:46.880
I'm mad at you, Smoker.

27
00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:48.310
Hina's mad.

28
00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:51.150
[SMOKER]
Care to elaborate on that?

29
00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:52.220
[HINA]
It's just that...

30
00:02:52.250 --> 00:02:55.890
You actually seem to be
happy about the Straw Hats

31
00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:56.960
getting away.

32
00:02:58.090 --> 00:02:59.220
[SMOKER]
Hmm.

33
00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:02.230
Me? Why would I be?

34
00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:03.900
[HINA]
Who knows.

35
00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:06.320
[COBRA]
At which point my
dearest Vivi said to me,

36
00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:07.590
in a very formal manner,

37
00:03:07.590 --> 00:03:10.260
"I have something important to
talk with you about, Daddy.

38
00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:12.030
I mean Father."

39
00:03:12.060 --> 00:03:14.160
At that moment, I remember thinking to myself,

40
00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:17.000
"King or no,
it makes no difference."

41
00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:21.000
No man gives up
the title "Daddy."

42
00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:24.110
[IGARAM]
Your Majesty,
what are you saying?

43
00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:27.110
[COBRA]
Watching children grow
is a bittersweet experience.

44
00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:40.020
[CHAKA]
Try as I might,
I cannot accept your death.

45
00:03:42.730 --> 00:03:44.690
Can't even shed one tear.

46
00:03:46.430 --> 00:03:48.060
Why is that?

47
00:03:48.100 --> 00:03:49.100
Old friend.

48
00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:01.440
[OFFICER]
Cannons fire!

49
00:04:09.250 --> 00:04:13.220
[TOTO laughing]

50
00:04:13.370 --> 00:04:15.070
[YUBA MAN]
What's so funny, Toto?

51
00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:17.140
You've been laughing ever since the speech.

52
00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:19.210
[KOZA]
Yeah. Let us in on
the joke, old man,

53
00:04:19.210 --> 00:04:21.040
'cause right now
we're in the dark.

54
00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:22.410
[TOTO laughs]
It's a secret!

55
00:04:22.440 --> 00:04:25.210
But trust me, guys, it's a good one.

56
00:04:25.210 --> 00:04:26.880
[KOZA]
You're not making any sense!

57
00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:28.220
[TOTO laughs]

58
00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:32.650
Now have a good journey, Luffy!

59
00:04:32.650 --> 00:04:35.420
You're welcome to drink
Yuba's water anytime!

60
00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:40.500
[TOTO laughing]

61
00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:42.300
All right, that's enough jawing.

62
00:04:42.330 --> 00:04:44.070
There's work to be done!

63
00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:45.640
Dig the well! Dig!

64
00:04:45.670 --> 00:04:47.640
[YUBA MAN]
Okay, okay.

65
00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:53.600
[NANOHANA 1]
Does anyone have
a clue who Princess Vivi

66
00:04:53.670 --> 00:04:55.210
was talking to?

67
00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:57.840
Nah, but who really cares anyway?

68
00:04:57.880 --> 00:05:00.040
[NANOHANA 3]
Yeah, what she
said makes us happy.

69
00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:02.210
[WOMAN A]
And it's our
duty to respond to it!

70
00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:04.220
She's right. Well said.

71
00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:06.140
Even though we're simply peasants.

72
00:05:06.210 --> 00:05:07.910
Speak for yourself, peasant!

73
00:05:07.940 --> 00:05:09.740
[ALL laugh]

74
00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:16.080
Waiting for that
one true dream...

75
00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:21.230
[RAINBASE 1]
As expected,
Alubarna seems to be

76
00:05:21.230 --> 00:05:22.560
in bad shape.

77
00:05:22.600 --> 00:05:24.600
[RAINBASE 2]
Perfect. We should go there.

78
00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:25.930
[RAINBASE 1]
But we also have to restore Yuba

79
00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:27.270
as quickly as possible.

80
00:05:27.270 --> 00:05:29.200
It's an important
crossroad in the west.

81
00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:31.040
[RAINBASE 2]
And don't forget
we still need to repair

82
00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:33.230
all the canals along the Sandora River.

83
00:05:33.260 --> 00:05:34.760
[RAINBASE 3]
What about the casino?

84
00:05:34.800 --> 00:05:35.800
[RAINBASE 2]
It'll be closed.

85
00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:36.830
Let's go, everyone!

86
00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:37.880
[RAINBASES]
Yeah!

87
00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:42.920
Um, why's he getting
special treatment?

88
00:05:42.920 --> 00:05:46.690
'Cause. Princess Vivi
told us to, I guess.

89
00:05:46.720 --> 00:05:49.520
He wants to join the Supersonic Duck Squadron.

90
00:05:52.760 --> 00:05:54.190
[SOLDIER]
He's a camel.

91
00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:55.550
What gave it away?

92
00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:00.690
[PELL]
Well I'm off.

93
00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:02.260
Thank you for everything.

94
00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:04.740
Too hasty for your
own good, huh!

95
00:06:04.770 --> 00:06:06.300
Someone with your
injuries shouldn't even be

96
00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:07.290
out of bed!

97
00:06:07.370 --> 00:06:08.410
[PELL]
I'll be fine.

98
00:06:08.440 --> 00:06:10.540
[DOCTOR]
Just promise me
that if you make it home,

99
00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:12.200
you'll take things easy and rest.

100
00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:13.600
[PELL]
Okay, I get it.

101
00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:16.580
[DOCTOR]
Hey, wait!

102
00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:19.710
[DOCTOR]
Here. You forgot this.

103
00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:21.880
[PELL]
Oh, thank you.

104
00:06:23.130 --> 00:06:24.470
everyone attacks!

105
00:06:29.140 --> 00:06:31.010
[LUFFY]
Okay! Now we ready?

106
00:06:33.610 --> 00:06:34.980
Now's our chance!

107
00:06:35.010 --> 00:06:36.610
Full-speed ahead! Shake 'em off!

108
00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:42.650
[VIVI]
Now, Karoo.

109
00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:43.990
[KAROO squawks]

110
00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:48.200
Let's go to Alubarna!

111
00:06:48.200 --> 00:07:01.390
if I'm to succeed in
bringing my homeland

112
00:07:01.390 --> 00:07:03.330
Hey, Captain Smoker.

113
00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:07.230
[SMOKER]
Tashigi. So how are your legs?

114
00:07:07.270 --> 00:07:08.370
They're doing fine.

115
00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:10.000
Change the subject.

116
00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:22.850
[TASHIGI]
Thank you.

117
00:07:24.900 --> 00:07:27.330
I saw the new bounties on their heads.

118
00:07:27.350 --> 00:07:30.400
[SMOKER]
The amount's no surprise
considering the catch.

119
00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:33.100
Have you heard what his swordsman buddy did?

120
00:07:33.110 --> 00:07:34.310
You mean Roronoa?

121
00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:38.520
He cut down one hundred bounty
hunters in Whisky Peak,

122
00:07:38.550 --> 00:07:42.990
and then, in Alubarna, he killed Daz Bones.

123
00:07:42.990 --> 00:07:45.330
The assassin? No way!

124
00:07:45.330 --> 00:07:47.300
[SMOKER]
He used to be a
bounty hunter and was known

125
00:07:47.330 --> 00:07:49.000
throughout the West Blue.

126
00:07:49.100 --> 00:07:52.580
In Baroque Works, he went
by the alias Mr. 1.

127
00:07:52.580 --> 00:07:55.320
Considering Crocodile had
so many famous warriors

128
00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:57.220
at his command,
you'd think they'd be

129
00:07:57.260 --> 00:07:59.900
unstoppable against
any opposition.

130
00:07:59.900 --> 00:08:03.560
However, fate was not kind.

131
00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:05.630
One day we'll have a rematch.

132
00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:06.600
Damn Straw Hats.

133
00:08:06.600 --> 00:08:09.580
[TASHIGI]
Yes, and I will
defeat you, Roronoa Zoro.

134
00:08:09.620 --> 00:08:11.780
[ZORO]
Looks like the Marines
have stopped following us.

135
00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:14.550
[GROUP groaning]

136
00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:16.960
[ZORO]
That's good news,
we shook 'em off!

137
00:08:16.990 --> 00:08:21.560
[GROUP groaning]

138
00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:22.350
Stop it!

139
00:08:22.350 --> 00:08:24.190
What's with the pathetic groans?

140
00:08:26.590 --> 00:08:28.830
I miss her!

141
00:08:28.860 --> 00:08:30.460
[ZORO]
That's enough whining!

142
00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:33.290
If you wanted her
to join that bad,

143
00:08:33.290 --> 00:08:35.130
then you shouldn't
have let her leave!

144
00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:36.530
Ah! You savage!

145
00:08:36.530 --> 00:08:37.560
Blockhead!

146
00:08:37.590 --> 00:08:38.550
Idiot.

147
00:08:38.600 --> 00:08:39.700
Three Swords Style.

148
00:08:39.700 --> 00:08:43.300
Saying "Three Swords Style"
isn't an insult, Luffy.

149
00:08:43.420 --> 00:08:44.420
Four Swords Style.

150
00:08:44.450 --> 00:08:45.520
[USOPP]
It's not the number
that's the problem.

151
00:08:45.540 --> 00:08:48.480
An effective insult must
involve some personal detail

152
00:08:48.570 --> 00:08:50.780
about the recipient that's
rude or disparaging!

153
00:08:50.810 --> 00:08:53.410
[ROBIN]
Looks like we finally
escaped the firing squad!

154
00:08:53.410 --> 00:08:54.650
[ZORO]
Yeah.

155
00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:55.750
Excellent work.

156
00:08:56.650 --> 00:08:57.580
[GROUP gasps]

157
00:08:57.580 --> 00:09:00.180
Here to avenge your friends?
Just try it!

158
00:09:00.250 --> 00:09:01.660
What the hell
are you doing here?!

159
00:09:01.660 --> 00:09:04.520
[USOPP]
– Warning. Warning.
[CHOPPER yelling]

160
00:09:06.490 --> 00:09:07.400
[CHOPPER]
Who's she?

161
00:09:07.400 --> 00:09:10.540
I don't know,
but she's so damn beautiful!

162
00:09:16.140 --> 00:09:17.440
[weapons clatter]

163
00:09:17.480 --> 00:09:18.810
Didn't I tell you before?

164
00:09:18.880 --> 00:09:21.210
Don't point such dangerous objects at me.

165
00:09:21.210 --> 00:09:22.700
Are you always so slow?

166
00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:24.570
How long have you been on our ship?

167
00:09:24.620 --> 00:09:26.280
[ROBIN]
Quite a while.

168
00:09:26.320 --> 00:09:29.220
These are your clothes, right?
I'm borrowing them.

169
00:09:29.260 --> 00:09:30.090
Just a minute, lady!

170
00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:31.910
Who in the hell
do you think you are?

171
00:09:31.910 --> 00:09:33.680
Monkey D. Luffy.

172
00:09:33.680 --> 00:09:35.580
It hasn't been so long
that you've forgotten

173
00:09:35.610 --> 00:09:36.750
what you did to me, has it?

174
00:09:36.780 --> 00:09:38.020
[SANJI growls]

175
00:09:38.020 --> 00:09:38.880
Luffy!

176
00:09:38.920 --> 00:09:40.620
What'd you do to
that beautiful woman,

177
00:09:40.650 --> 00:09:42.580
you lousy bastard?
Tell me! Confess!

178
00:09:42.630 --> 00:09:45.800
[USOPP]
All stowaways must
leave the ship immediately!

179
00:09:45.830 --> 00:09:47.800
Wait a minute! Stop lying!

180
00:09:47.800 --> 00:09:49.700
You know I didn't do anything to you!

181
00:09:49.700 --> 00:09:50.530
Wrong.

182
00:09:50.600 --> 00:09:53.100
And what you did to me was unbearable.

183
00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:55.700
Go ahead. Admit it.

184
00:09:55.770 --> 00:09:58.140
[CHOPPER]
Who's that woman
and what's she talking about?

185
00:09:58.170 --> 00:09:59.970
[USOPP]
...all mystery chicks
vacate the ship

186
00:09:59.980 --> 00:10:01.620
or we'll be forced
to call the Marines.

187
00:10:01.650 --> 00:10:03.120
Thank you for voyaging
on the Going Merry.

188
00:10:03.150 --> 00:10:04.290
[SANJI]
...tear you apart!

189
00:10:04.320 --> 00:10:07.760
You're not makin' any sense.
What do you want me to do?

190
00:10:09.520 --> 00:10:11.860
I want to join you.

191
00:10:12.100 --> 00:10:13.370
[GROUP]
– What?!
– What?!

192
00:10:17.380 --> 00:10:19.080
[ROBIN]
Use that, immediately!

193
00:10:19.110 --> 00:10:22.550
It can neutralize the poison from Crocodile's hook.

194
00:10:22.550 --> 00:10:24.250
Even if he was buried in this rubble,

195
00:10:24.280 --> 00:10:25.550
there's a chance
he might survive

196
00:10:25.580 --> 00:10:27.450
since he's actually rubber.

197
00:10:29.440 --> 00:10:31.470
[COBRA]
You looked me straight
in the eye and told me

198
00:10:31.510 --> 00:10:34.310
that the only thing
written here was history!

199
00:10:37.780 --> 00:10:39.620
Why did you lie to me?

200
00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:43.800
You knew?

201
00:10:43.800 --> 00:10:45.400
How cruel.

202
00:10:45.430 --> 00:10:47.770
[COBRA]
The truth is, this
country's history isn't written

203
00:10:47.820 --> 00:10:49.290
anywhere in there.

204
00:10:49.320 --> 00:10:51.260
Instead, it has everything
about the weapon

205
00:10:51.320 --> 00:10:53.150
you wanted to get your hands on.

206
00:10:53.160 --> 00:10:55.230
The description, location.

207
00:10:55.260 --> 00:10:56.760
It doesn't make any sense.

208
00:10:56.790 --> 00:10:58.660
If you had told Crocodile this information,

209
00:10:58.740 --> 00:11:01.070
this country would now
be his for the taking.

210
00:11:01.110 --> 00:11:02.170
Isn't that right?

211
00:11:03.730 --> 00:11:05.360
I'm not interested.

212
00:11:05.400 --> 00:11:08.210
Whether people in
this country live or die...

213
00:11:08.210 --> 00:11:10.780
It really makes no difference to me.

214
00:11:10.870 --> 00:11:12.770
I had already decided from the start

215
00:11:12.840 --> 00:11:15.380
not to give Crocodile the weapon.

216
00:11:15.460 --> 00:11:16.890
[COBRA]
I don't understand.

217
00:11:16.930 --> 00:11:19.750
Then why did you come here?

218
00:11:19.750 --> 00:11:22.920
I don't really know anymore.

219
00:11:22.950 --> 00:11:25.390
Chasing a dream, I suppose.

220
00:11:25.420 --> 00:11:26.560
An empty dream.

221
00:11:28.390 --> 00:11:30.530
The last remaining Poneglyph in the world

222
00:11:30.530 --> 00:11:33.530
that still carries the true history.

223
00:11:36.820 --> 00:11:39.220
The Rio Poneglyph.

224
00:11:39.290 --> 00:11:40.790
What do you mean by

225
00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:42.340
the "true history"?

226
00:11:44.240 --> 00:11:45.800
[ROBIN]
Nothing.

227
00:11:45.800 --> 00:11:47.400
It doesn't matter now.

228
00:11:47.460 --> 00:11:48.700
For 20 years I've searched,

229
00:11:48.730 --> 00:11:51.470
and I've never had a better lead than this.

230
00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:53.300
This was my last hope.

231
00:11:53.350 --> 00:11:54.900
And it didn't work out.

232
00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:58.310
So if I'm going to die here, it's the perfect time.

233
00:11:58.340 --> 00:12:00.510
I'm tired of this fool's crusade.

234
00:12:00.510 --> 00:12:01.880
It's over.

235
00:12:06.420 --> 00:12:09.420
All I wanted was
to learn our true history

236
00:12:11.520 --> 00:12:14.660
and to share it with
the whole world.

237
00:12:16.370 --> 00:12:17.840
So then, you're saying

238
00:12:17.870 --> 00:12:19.940
that it's possible our lost
history could actually

239
00:12:19.950 --> 00:12:20.820
be uncovered?

240
00:12:20.830 --> 00:12:23.130
And the Poneglyphs
are the key to unlocking

241
00:12:23.130 --> 00:12:24.160
these records?

242
00:12:26.350 --> 00:12:28.820
[COBRA]
You mean, all this time...

243
00:12:34.660 --> 00:12:35.930
'Kay. Let's go.

244
00:12:35.990 --> 00:12:37.500
[ROBIN]
Hold on!

245
00:12:37.500 --> 00:12:39.430
I no longer have
a reason to live!

246
00:12:39.500 --> 00:12:42.030
Just leave me here!

247
00:12:42.070 --> 00:12:43.000
You're coming with me.

248
00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:45.840
Do what you want once we're out of here.

249
00:12:47.740 --> 00:12:49.280
[ROBIN]
I wanted nothing
more than to die

250
00:12:49.340 --> 00:12:51.010
at that very moment.

251
00:12:51.010 --> 00:12:52.440
But you forced me to live.

252
00:12:52.510 --> 00:12:54.680
That's your crime!

253
00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:57.720
There's no place for me to go, or return to.

254
00:12:57.750 --> 00:13:00.120
So I've decided
that I'll join you.

255
00:13:00.210 --> 00:13:03.140
I see your problem.
Guess there's no other choice.

256
00:13:03.210 --> 00:13:05.760
– Welcome.
[GROUP]
– Luffy!

257
00:13:05.760 --> 00:13:07.430
There's nothing to worry about.

258
00:13:07.550 --> 00:13:09.920
Trust me.
She isn't a bad person.

259
00:13:22.960 --> 00:13:25.500
[laughing]

260
00:13:32.170 --> 00:13:33.440
[USOPP]
Pay attention!

261
00:13:33.440 --> 00:13:36.110
I want some straight-up
and honest answers!

262
00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:37.810
I'll ask you one more time.

263
00:13:37.810 --> 00:13:38.880
What's your name?

264
00:13:40.410 --> 00:13:43.050
My name's Usopp. Hello.

265
00:13:43.120 --> 00:13:44.280
Nico Robin.

266
00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:45.820
Okay, Nico Robin.

267
00:13:45.850 --> 00:13:47.380
So what's your occupation?

268
00:13:47.470 --> 00:13:48.570
Archaeologist.

269
00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:50.070
Are you serious?

270
00:13:50.140 --> 00:13:52.240
Archaeology runs in my blood.

271
00:13:52.310 --> 00:13:54.040
I come from a long line of them.

272
00:13:54.380 --> 00:13:56.310
It was when I was 8 years old

273
00:13:56.340 --> 00:13:59.380
that I decided to pursue
archaeology as my career.

274
00:13:59.450 --> 00:14:00.650
Shortly
thereafter,

275
00:14:00.680 --> 00:14:03.120
I found myself wanted
by the World Government.

276
00:14:03.120 --> 00:14:04.990
Since then I've spent
the past 20 years

277
00:14:05.020 --> 00:14:06.490
hiding from the world.

278
00:14:06.520 --> 00:14:08.460
You've been alone?

279
00:14:08.510 --> 00:14:10.180
Ever since you were 8?

280
00:14:11.710 --> 00:14:13.250
Then one day,

281
00:14:13.280 --> 00:14:14.750
I heard the calling of the sea,

282
00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:16.600
but there's no way
for a child to survive

283
00:14:16.630 --> 00:14:17.670
alone on the water.

284
00:14:17.730 --> 00:14:20.340
The only option I found
that ensured my protection

285
00:14:20.400 --> 00:14:22.670
and the ability to
achieve my goal was...

286
00:14:22.740 --> 00:14:24.440
I chose to work
for various rogues.

287
00:14:24.470 --> 00:14:27.310
Not an ideal solution,
but it brought me this far.

288
00:14:27.340 --> 00:14:28.580
And here we are.

289
00:14:29.500 --> 00:14:31.130
I'm good at maneuvering
through obstacles

290
00:14:31.130 --> 00:14:32.640
to achieve a goal.

291
00:14:32.670 --> 00:14:35.140
I'd be a great asset to you and your friends.

292
00:14:35.170 --> 00:14:37.980
Huh. You're full of confidence.

293
00:14:38.010 --> 00:14:39.480
What's your specialty?

294
00:14:41.810 --> 00:14:42.810
Killing.

295
00:14:42.850 --> 00:14:45.650
Luffy! My investigation
has concluded that she is

296
00:14:45.680 --> 00:14:46.820
far too dangerous!

297
00:14:46.850 --> 00:14:48.520
[LUFFY, CHOPPER laughing]

298
00:14:48.520 --> 00:14:48.880
but there's no way
for a child to survive

299
00:14:48.880 --> 00:14:49.580
alone on the water.

300
00:14:52.280 --> 00:14:54.690
I'm disappointed.
You two are pathetic!

301
00:14:54.690 --> 00:14:56.750
Until recently, she was
the vice president

302
00:14:56.790 --> 00:14:58.690
of a crime syndicate.

303
00:14:58.690 --> 00:15:02.630
And you really think such a woman should join us?

304
00:15:02.690 --> 00:15:04.560
You may've fooled these idiots,

305
00:15:04.600 --> 00:15:06.430
but I'm not convinced!

306
00:15:06.480 --> 00:15:10.880
You pull anything, and I'll
personally kick you out!

307
00:15:10.910 --> 00:15:11.950
All right.

308
00:15:11.980 --> 00:15:13.980
I'll keep that in mind.

309
00:15:14.050 --> 00:15:15.920
Oh, I just remembered.

310
00:15:15.950 --> 00:15:18.420
I brought along some of Crocodile's jewelry with me.

311
00:15:19.720 --> 00:15:20.890
[NAMI squeals]

312
00:15:20.890 --> 00:15:23.390
Wow, I love ya, sister!
You're the best!

313
00:15:23.390 --> 00:15:25.160
[USOPP, ZORO]
– Oh, boy, here we go.
– Oh, boy, here we go.

314
00:15:25.160 --> 00:15:26.460
Nami's been had.

315
00:15:26.460 --> 00:15:27.790
This chick's bad news.

316
00:15:27.830 --> 00:15:30.460
She's following her lead
like some kinda pet!

317
00:15:33.530 --> 00:15:36.140
Ah, love. Bold.

318
00:15:36.180 --> 00:15:37.710
The likes of which I've never seen.

319
00:15:37.790 --> 00:15:39.630
I'm captured by your spell.

320
00:15:39.700 --> 00:15:41.900
Held prisoner in your eyes.

321
00:15:41.930 --> 00:15:42.750
[NAMI]
Treasure!

322
00:15:42.750 --> 00:15:44.720
[SANJI]
I was driftwood floating at sea

323
00:15:44.770 --> 00:15:46.500
until you struck me
like a thunderbolt

324
00:15:46.540 --> 00:15:48.800
igniting my soul.

325
00:15:48.870 --> 00:15:50.200
A snack.

326
00:15:50.210 --> 00:15:51.680
Ah, thank you.

327
00:15:51.710 --> 00:15:53.770
[ZORO]
Look at him. Falling
all over himself.

328
00:15:53.770 --> 00:15:54.670
[USOPP]
Yeah.

329
00:15:54.700 --> 00:15:57.370
Well, he was a lost
cause from the start.

330
00:15:57.440 --> 00:15:59.310
[ZORO sighs]

331
00:15:59.420 --> 00:16:01.190
Looks like you and
I are the only holdouts

332
00:16:01.220 --> 00:16:03.260
on this ship of insanity.

333
00:16:03.290 --> 00:16:04.500
We shouldn't blame the others.

334
00:16:04.500 --> 00:16:06.570
Their simple minds can't resist her charms.

335
00:16:06.610 --> 00:16:07.740
[LUFFY]
Hey, Usopp!

336
00:16:08.610 --> 00:16:09.680
Chopper.

337
00:16:09.740 --> 00:16:10.940
[CHOPPER laughing]

338
00:16:10.980 --> 00:16:15.210
[LUFFY, NAMI, CHOPPER]

339
00:16:16.790 --> 00:16:18.550
[SANJI]
What should I call you? "Robin"?

340
00:16:18.550 --> 00:16:21.220
Or something more daring that declares my love?

341
00:16:22.820 --> 00:16:23.820
Leaving?

342
00:16:27.390 --> 00:16:28.490
[SANJI sighs]

343
00:16:28.560 --> 00:16:29.660
She's great!

344
00:16:29.730 --> 00:16:31.330
With an adult charm.

345
00:16:31.400 --> 00:16:33.260
She's far different than Nami.

346
00:16:38.400 --> 00:16:40.570
This ship has charm.

347
00:16:40.600 --> 00:16:43.310
Is it always this lively?

348
00:16:43.340 --> 00:16:45.340
Yeah, it usually is.

349
00:16:49.510 --> 00:16:51.480
[ZORO]
This woman's up to something.

350
00:16:51.520 --> 00:16:52.590
But what?

351
00:16:58.500 --> 00:17:00.270
What's the forecast, Navigator?

352
00:17:00.310 --> 00:17:01.680
Is it smooth sailing ahead?

353
00:17:01.710 --> 00:17:04.440
[NAMI]
The wind is calm
and the weather's beautiful.

354
00:17:04.470 --> 00:17:06.610
There's no problems
on my end, Sis!

355
00:17:06.640 --> 00:17:08.440
[ZORO]
How would you know?
You haven't stopped gawking

356
00:17:08.480 --> 00:17:09.280
at that jewelry!

357
00:17:09.280 --> 00:17:11.610
[LUFFY]
Sanji! Is our snack ready?

358
00:17:11.610 --> 00:17:12.650
[SANJI]
Be patient!
